        <body>
            <div xml:id="d591-a14">

                <pb facs="0566" n="492" xml:id="pg492"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#center">[Telegram.—<placeName>Corunna</placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-02-13">February 13,
                        1865</date>.]</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Perry, American Chargé d’Affaires:</hi></p>
                <p>Pledges were given by the French government to our late Minister Dayton that the
                    ram should not be transferred to the rebels. Cannot Bigelow, at Paris, obtain
                    the intervention of French, with that of the Spanish government, to arrest the
                    ram now fitting out at Ferrol, or to detain her until her ease has been
                    thoroughly investigated?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CRAVEN, <hi rendition="#italic">Commanding the
                    Niagara.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
